    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Column {width=\"30%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "In the bar chart, from the 5 selected countries, Sierra Leone and Nigeriaa shows to have high child mortality rates from 2010. \n",
        "\n",
        "Senegal seems to have the lowest death rates from 2010 to 2020 perhaps due to rapid child immunization campaigns.\n",
        "\n",
        "The rates slowly declines, perhaps due to immunisation practices, such as polio, for children and aggressive immunization campagins against childhood diseases.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# About\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal**\n",
        "\n",
        "In this final project, I will display relationships between child mortality, and under 5 population (0-5 years).\n",
        "\n",
        "The goal is to clean and merge these raw datasets and produce tables and charts with the data.\n",
        "\n",
        "The data was downloaded from Gapminder and the goal of this projec to produce a report with three pages:\n",
        "\n",
        "- First Indicator Analysis\n",
        "- Second Indicator Analysis\n",
        "- Relationship between the two indicators. No statistical analysis is required; this can be purely descriptive/graphical.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data Import**\n",
        "\n",
        "I have imported 2 *raw* datasets, 'child_mortality_0_5_years' and 'under 5 population' accessed from Gapminder Foundation.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Child Mortality from 0 to 5 years**. (*data/child_mortality_0_5_year_olds_dying_per_1000_born.csv*).\n",
        "\n",
        "According to Gapminder description, child mortality is the probability of dying between birth and exactly five years of age expressed in 1000 live births.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Under Five Population**. (*data/u5pop.csv*).\n",
        "\n",
        "According to Gapminder description, is the total number of children, aged 0-4 years old.\n",
        "\n",
        "Loading the datasets into Python using 'pd.read_csv' to have an idea of the data structure."
      ],
      "id": "dc35bbf3"
    }
